1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,620
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,970
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:06,040
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:08,500
I've been a machinist for
thirty years.

5
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:09,470
Standing at a lathe

6
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:11,060
on a concrete shop floor,

7
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,150
the whole shift.

8
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,090
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,090 --> 00:00:14,580
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:14,790 --> 00:00:16,960
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:18,660
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:20,320
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,340
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:22,650
This is different.

15
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:23,340
Tight.

16
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:24,140
Full.

17
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:25,020
Like a band around

18
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,720
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:27,660
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:28,970
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,070
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:32,210
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:33,760
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:34,660
At three months,

25
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:35,720
give it six.

26
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:36,910
At six months,

27
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:38,700
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:39,880
At a year,

29
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,610
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,730 --> 00:00:42,710
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:43,920
We went down the list.

32
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,480
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,690 --> 00:00:46,800
Every session,

34
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,430
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:49,920
I got stronger.

36
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,540
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:52,960
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,310
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,510 --> 00:00:56,560
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:57,740
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:59,090
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,080
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,460
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:05,140
And after that, a second

45
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,370
operation to go back

46
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:07,950
in and do it over.

47
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:09,450
I said no.

48
00:01:09,550 --> 00:01:11,540
Every morning I walked
into the shop

49
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:12,660
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,450
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:16,790
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:18,120
Every morning

53
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:18,780
I took something

54
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:20,530
for it and went to work.

55
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:22,110
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:23,190
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:23,190 --> 00:01:24,820
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:26,310
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

59
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:28,910
game without shifting
every two minutes.

60
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:30,140
By lunch

61
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:32,150
I'd be leaning on the
lathe just

62
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:33,800
to take the weight off
that leg.

63
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,970
The guys at the shop
started carrying

64
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,190
the heavy stock for me.

65
00:01:37,230 --> 00:01:38,570
Nobody said anything.

66
00:01:38,910 --> 00:01:40,340
It woke me at night,

67
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:41,720
and it turned ordinary
things,

68
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:43,080
like getting in the car

69
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,350
or up off the couch,

70
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:45,370
into a decision.

71
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,160
After a long and serious

72
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,430
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:50,230
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:51,430
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:52,770
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,790
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:54,790 --> 00:01:56,790
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:56,830 --> 00:01:58,910
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:01:58,910 --> 00:01:59,840
nothing wrong.

80
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,360
Only this time there

81
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,600
was no new number.

82
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,900
Nobody said give it
another six months.

83
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:06,490
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:07,670
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:08,560
lot for a while.

86
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:09,340
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:10,570
Then explain this.

88
00:02:10,850 --> 00:02:12,940
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:14,400
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:16,780
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,930
Everyone in the house was
asleep

92
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,680
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

93
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:21,790
with my leg up,

94
00:02:21,790 --> 00:02:23,430
trying to find any angle
where

95
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:24,540
it didn't feel like
something

96
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:27,080
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

97
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,720
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

98
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:31,540
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

99
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,690
And I just thought,

100
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:34,160
is this really my life
now?

101
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,560
I can't live like this.

102
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:37,260
So I made myself a
promise.

103
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:37,970
I wouldn't go a day

104
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:39,380
without looking for an
answer.

105
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:41,120
And when I found one,

106
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,150
I'd share it with everyone

107
00:02:42,150 --> 00:02:43,390
going through the same
thing.

108
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:44,440
So I got my laptop

109
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,380
out and went looking.

110
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:46,610
Not for a product.

111
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:48,070
For an explanation.

112
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:49,860
Mayo Clinic forums,

113
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:52,170
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

114
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:54,700
doctor videos, medical
animations.

115
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,110
And that's when I found a
video

116
00:02:56,110 --> 00:02:57,780
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

117
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,030
Steven Salinger,

118
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:00,120
whose own wife had been

119
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:01,470
through exactly this.

120
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:03,420
But before I say anything
else,

121
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:04,960
I want to be straight with
you.

122
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,590
You've already had
something work fast.

123
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:08,400
The ice.

124
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,110
The first week of a new
pill.

125
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:11,990
The good day after a
session.

126
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,240
Then it wore off.

127
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:15,520
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

128
00:03:15,810 --> 00:03:17,700
Fast relief isn't relief.

129
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,920
It's a preview.

130
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,070
So I'm not going to tell

131
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:21,290
you this works fast.

132
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:22,190
It doesn't.

133
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:23,780
But if you're willing to
be patient,

134
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:24,480
and to look at what's

135
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,490
going on around your new

136
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:27,190
knee instead of inside it,

137
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:28,710
there is a real reason

138
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:29,820
it still hurts.

139
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,760
And something you can do
about it.

140
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,110
Let me explain what he
said,

141
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:34,370
because this is what
changed

142
00:03:34,370 --> 00:03:35,390
everything for me.

143
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,160
He started with the
basics.

144
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:38,630
A knee replacement takes
out

145
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:40,120
the worn joint surfaces

146
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,850
and puts in metal and
plastic.

147
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,730
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

148
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:45,290
you had before the
operation.

149
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:46,870
That part I already knew.

150
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:48,360
But then he explained
something

151
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:49,800
nobody had ever told me.

152
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:50,700
He said,

153
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,040
think about a swollen foot

154
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,050
inside a shoe.

155
00:03:53,090 --> 00:03:54,450
The shoe didn't shrink.

156
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,860
Your foot is taking up
more room,

157
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:58,630
so everything feels
cramped

158
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:00,230
and tight and squeezed.

159
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,720
Your new knee sits

160
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:03,410
in a limited space with
living

161
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:05,300
tissue packed all around
it.

162
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,680
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

163
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,550
had to work through that
tissue.

164
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:12,200
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

165
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,860
At first that's normal.

166
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:16,140
But in some people that
swelling can

167
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:19,690
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

168
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:21,970
And swollen tissue takes
up more

169
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,950
room than calm tissue
does.

170
00:04:24,090 --> 00:04:25,290
So when you bend,

171
00:04:25,290 --> 00:04:27,320
that tissue gets
compressed.

172
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,600
When you straighten,

173
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,860
it gets pulled tight.

174
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:31,000
That's the band.

175
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:33,380
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

176
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:34,410
And you start being

177
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:35,600
the one who says,

178
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,620
you go ahead.

179
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:37,650
I'll stay here.

180
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:39,600
And that's exactly why so
much

181
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,470
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

182
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:44,070
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

183
00:04:44,070 --> 00:04:45,050
around the knee.

184
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:46,180
Worth doing,

185
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:47,140
and I'd done it.

186
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,740
It does nothing about
tissue

187
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:49,780
taking up room.

188
00:04:49,970 --> 00:04:51,130
A nerve block quiets

189
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:52,740
the nerve carrying the
signal.

190
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:54,800
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

191
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:56,890
But when that irritated
tissue

192
00:04:56,890 --> 00:04:58,290
finally calms down,

193
00:04:58,290 --> 00:04:59,760
it holds less fluid,

194
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:01,440
and it takes up less room.

195
00:05:01,790 --> 00:05:03,740
Less room taken up means

196
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:05,980
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

197
00:05:06,050 --> 00:05:08,010
That's what takes the
pressure off.

198
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:09,780
After two years of this,

199
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:11,390
it finally made sense.

200
00:05:11,690 --> 00:05:13,610
The problem was never the
new knee.

201
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:15,660
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

202
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:17,530
He calls it the squeeze.

203
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:20,060
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

204
00:05:20,330 --> 00:05:22,030
I'd bought knee sleeves,

205
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,450
anti-fatigue mats,

206
00:05:23,450 --> 00:05:25,890
compression braces,
creams,

207
00:05:25,890 --> 00:05:27,680
half of Amazon really,

208
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:28,920
and all any of it gave

209
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:29,990
me was an hour.

210
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:30,970
I even looked at going

211
00:05:30,970 --> 00:05:32,700
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

212
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,550
But at $200 a session

213
00:05:34,550 --> 00:05:36,650
with nothing covered by
insurance,

214
00:05:36,650 --> 00:05:37,950
that was a quick no.

215
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:40,030
Then one night I went back

216
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:41,780
to that knee replacement
group

217
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:42,890
and actually read it.

218
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,850
Thousands of people,

219
00:05:44,850 --> 00:05:46,380
years out from surgery,

220
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:49,190
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

221
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:50,620
nobody could explain.

222
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,910
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

223
00:05:52,910 --> 00:05:54,560
the same thing kept coming
up.

224
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,460
This one device,

225
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,720
and people saying it was
the first

226
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,990
thing that made a
difference.

227
00:06:01,350 --> 00:06:03,640
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

228
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,230
alright, here it comes,

229
00:06:05,230 --> 00:06:06,810
he's selling me something,

230
00:06:06,810 --> 00:06:08,670
let me shut that down
right now.

231
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:10,710
I'm only here because I
made myself

232
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:12,970
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

233
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:14,040
that if I ever found

234
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,230
something that helped,

235
00:06:15,230 --> 00:06:16,240
I'd say so.

236
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,240
It's called the KenRelief
Red

237
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:19,600
Light Therapy Wrap.

238
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,730
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

239
00:06:22,010 --> 00:06:24,250
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

240
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:26,680
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

241
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:28,910
But I went to their
website anyway,

242
00:06:28,910 --> 00:06:29,800
just to see what all

243
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,110
the fuss was about.

244
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:34,470
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

245
00:06:34,470 --> 00:06:37,550
charge $200 a session for,

246
00:06:37,550 --> 00:06:40,690
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

247
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:41,780
in a wrap you plug

248
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:43,130
into the wall at home.

249
00:06:43,170 --> 00:06:44,900
Two hundred and forty
lights.

250
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,990
Red at 660 nanometers

251
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:49,330
and near-infrared at 850,

252
00:06:49,330 --> 00:06:51,550
run together for the
strongest effect.

253
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:53,030
Four strength levels.

254
00:06:53,070 --> 00:06:54,980
A five to thirty minute
timer.

255
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:56,560
Then I saw the guarantee.

256
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,750
Ninety days.

257
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,640
Results or your money
back,

258
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:02,090
no questions, no store
credit,

259
00:07:02,090 --> 00:07:03,810
and you don't even send it
back.

260
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:06,830
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

261
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:08,400
days to change my mind.

262
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:10,150
There wasn't much to lose,

263
00:07:10,150 --> 00:07:11,290
so I ordered it.

264
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:12,800
Two of them, actually.

265
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:15,330
Only the right knee was
replaced,

266
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:17,400
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

267
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:18,750
and I'd done it at the
lathe

268
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:19,860
for two years.

269
00:07:19,930 --> 00:07:21,890
The left one was carrying
the difference.

270
00:07:22,070 --> 00:07:23,110
When it came,

271
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:25,670
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

272
00:07:25,670 --> 00:07:27,100
because I'd been let down
too

273
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:28,830
many times to get excited.

274
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:30,770
What I felt was warmth.

275
00:07:30,810 --> 00:07:32,530
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

276
00:07:32,810 --> 00:07:34,470
More like it was coming
from inside

277
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:36,020
the knee and spreading
around it.

278
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:36,940
And that was it.

279
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:38,920
That was the whole
experience.

280
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:40,310
When I took it off,

281
00:07:40,310 --> 00:07:41,300
I'll be honest,

282
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,910
nothing dramatic had
happened.

283
